Topics and json format for childs´ Arduino - publisher (both backend and parent Arduino are subsribers):

child/telemetry:
{
"temperature_c": 00.0,
"humidity_pct": 00.0,
"light_level": "very_low"/"low"/"medium"/ "high"/"very_high"
 "timestamp": "2026-11-17T11:20:00Z"
}

child/event/duration:
{
"event_id": 1795074236,
"type": "sleep"/"walk",
"action": "start"/"stop",
 "timestamp": "2026-11-17T11:20:00Z"
}

child/event/instant:
{
"event_id": 1795074240,
"type": "eat"/"diaper",
"timestamp": "2026-11-17T11:20:00Z"
}

event_id = Unix time in seconds when the button is pressed (integer, WiFi.getTime()). The same event_id for start and stop.

Backend sands to parents´ Arduino, if connection was lost (retained, only on change):

child/status
{
  "state": "offline",
  "last_seen": "2026-11-17T14:40:00Z"
}

{
  "state": "online"
}

Parent Arduino subscriber to all 4 topics. It checks temperature_c / humidity_pct from child/telemetry against limits in its own code (no extra topic).
